🚨 Kubernetes Common Errors & Fixes 🚨

Master these to keep your clusters clean and your apps running! ⚙️🐳


---

1️⃣ ImagePullBackOff

🧩 Root Cause:

Image not found in registry ❌

Wrong image tag or name 🏷️

Private registry access failure 🔐


🛠️ Fix:

✅ Double-check the registry URL, image name, and tag.

🔑 For private registries, create a Kubernetes secret and link it in the deployment manifest.



---

2️⃣ CrashLoopBackOff

🧩 Root Cause:

Container process crashes immediately 💥

Resource (CPU/Memory) exhaustion 🧠💻


🛠️ Fix:

✅ Ensure proper resources.requests and resources.limits in the YAML.

🔍 Check logs with kubectl logs <pod-name>.



---

3️⃣ OOMKilled (Out Of Memory)

🧩 Root Cause:

POD exceeds memory limit 📈

Container gets terminated by Kubelet 🧹


🛠️ Fix:

✅ Re-adjust memory limits/requests in your YAML file.

🧪 Monitor app memory usage over time.



---

4️⃣ Pod Status: Pending

🧩 Root Cause:

Nodes are not ready ⚠️

Not enough CPU/Memory in the cluster 🚫


🛠️ Fix:

🔄 Scale the cluster or optimize resource requests.

🔍 Check with kubectl describe pod.



---

5️⃣ Pod Status: Waiting

🧩 Root Cause:

Image issues (again!) 🚫

Auth or pull errors from the registry


🛠️ Fix:

🔐 Recheck image credentials and registry secrets.

✅ Correct the image name/tag.



---

6️⃣ App Not Accessible Despite Pod Running

🧩 Root Cause:

No service created or service misconfigured ❌

App and service in different namespaces 🧭


🛠️ Fix:

🔧 Create proper Service (NodePort/ClusterIP/LoadBalancer).

✅ Ensure same namespace for both app and service.



---

7️⃣ Pod Status: Evicted

🧩 Root Cause:

Node runs out of disk or memory 🧹💾


🛠️ Fix:

📏 Set accurate resource requests/limits.

🧱 Add more capacity or redistribute workloads.



---

💡 Pro Tip: Always use kubectl describe pod <pod-name> and kubectl logs <pod-name> to troubleshoot smarter! 🔍💬
